BT 1 0 0 1 0 159 Tm /F3 11 Tf 17 TL -0.015906 Tw (In the village of Rotoava, on the leeward side of Fakarava atoll, there is a particular form of) Tj T* 0 Tw .25327 Tw (quiet that elders call nooanoa. It is not the absence of sound -- the reef breaks constantly at) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.403094 Tw (the outer edge, and the palms are rarely still -- but a held quality in the breath between) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.854276 Tw (speaker and listener that signals, without words, that something difficult is about to be) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.153661 Tw (named. I first encountered nooanoa in 2007, during a funeral preparation I had stumbled) Tj T* 0 Tw .891383 Tw (into uninvited. A woman named Teura sat across from her sister-in-law without speaking) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.000493 Tw (for forty minutes while three other women moved around them, washing dishes and folding) Tj T* 0 Tw .541892 Tw (cloth. When I asked my interpreter what the two women were communicating, she looked) Tj T* 0 Tw .699614 Tw (at me for a moment and said simply: 'Everything that matters.' That exchange became the) Tj T* 0 Tw (organizing question of this book.) Tj T* ET
