BT 1 0 0 1 0 108 Tm /F3 11 Tf 17 TL 24 0 Td .506732 Tw (Anthropologists have long been uncomfortable with silence. The discipline's primary) Tj T* 0 Tw -24 0 Td .078299 Tw (methods -- interview, observation, transcription -- are built for language. Silence appears in) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.096912 Tw (the record, when it appears at all, as a gap: an absence of utterance, a failure of the recorder,) Tj T* 0 Tw .485299 Tw (a moment before meaning begins. This book argues for a different understanding. Silence,) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.001024 Tw (in the Pacific communities I have studied, is not a gap. It is a medium -- structured, socially) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.159706 Tw (embedded, and as subject to convention and violation as any spoken form. My aim is to) Tj T* 0 Tw (develop a vocabulary adequate to describe it.) Tj T* ET
